---
import ExampleChoices from './ExampleChoices.astro';
const hosts = [
  { name:'Claude Code', command:'/ca:feature "export saved searches"', description:'Plugin commands and agents, trusted hooks, and an optional settings-wired statusline. Typed prompt approval exists; typed verification and review authority are not supported by the current production adapters.' },
  { name:'Codex', command:'$ca-feature "export saved searches"', description:'Codex-native skills, trusted hook handlers, and packaged role resources. Current source implements typed prompt, verification and review authority adapters here; the exact installed release still needs qualified capability.' },
  { name:'Pi', command:'/ca-feature "export saved searches"', description:'Generated aliases, project trust, a rich footer, and child work mediated by the parent adapter. Typed prompt approval, verification and review authority are not supported; native HTML capability alone cannot clear those stops.' },
];
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<div class="ca-host-views ca-exhibit" data-example="hosts">
  <p class="ca-kicker">One repository. Native entry points.</p>
  <ExampleChoices label="Compare host entry points" labels={hosts.map((host) => host.name)}>
    {hosts.map((host) => <section data-pane><h3>{host.name}</h3><pre tabindex="0"><code>{host.command}</code></pre><p>{host.description}</p>
      <p><strong>Shared project records:</strong> <code>.codearbiter/specs/</code>, <code>.codearbiter/plans/</code>, decisions, tasks and audit history.</p>
    </section>)}
  </ExampleChoices>
  <p class="ca-exhibit-footnote">Syntax comparison, not captured host output or proof of identical capabilities. Understood intent can route without typing a command. Installed support, trust and artifact capability still apply; this does not demonstrate simultaneous editing.</p>
  <p>Check <a href={`${base}/guides/review-artifacts/#check-your-hosts-authority-capability`}>typed-artifact authority by host</a> and <a href={`${base}/getting-started/compatibility/`}>supported platform differences</a> before execution.</p>
</div>
